  "term": "olfactory receptor",
  "definition": "An olfactory receptor is a protein on the cilia of smell receptor neurons that binds specific odor molecules and starts a response in the neuron. Many different olfactory receptors exist, and they appear to come from multiple gene families or subfamilies.",
